      "title": "Resolving Intermittent Service Failures Due to Unsupported Configurations",
      "content_summary": "Troubleshooting steps for applications experiencing intermittent failures, crashes, or unresponsiveness caused by unsupported configurations.",
      "content_body": "When a service exhibits intermittent failure or crashes without a clear root cause, first verify the current setup against documented support matrices. Many issues stem from unsupported configurations that cause instability rather than code defects. Gather full diagnostic logs to rule out engineering faults before proceeding. If an unsupported setting is identified, guide the customer to revert to a supported configuration. Escalate to engineering only if the failure persists after validation of the environment, otherwise close as a duplicate if linked to known configuration issues."
